.TH SAPHIRA-REPO-STATE 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-repo-state \- read-only repository.db viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-repo-state
.RB [ --gen " " NAME ]
.RI COMMAND " [" ARGS ]
.PP
Commands:
.BR summary ,
.BR packages ,
.BI package " NAME" ,
.BI owner " PATH" ,
.BR users ,
.BI user " NAME" ,
.BI gid " N" ,
.BI history " NAME" ,
.BR conflicts ,
.BR audit .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-repo-state
is the human interface to
.IR repository.db :
package identities, file ownership, Unix-identity reservations and
ledger history without writing SQL. It opens the database read-only
and contains no write path; all state changes flow through
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-repo-migrate (8),
.BR promote-repo
and
.BR seed-repo
only.
.B --gen
defaults to the live generation.
.B conflicts
lists newest-view multi-owner paths (legacy pairs, tolerated until
a staged package claims the path);
.B audit
verifies freshness read-only and never heals (healing is
.IR "sign-apk-repo --full-audit" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --gen " NAME"
Generation repository to inspect (default: the live one).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/<generation>/$ARCH/repository.db
The inspected database (never modified by this tool).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Answered.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown package, user, path, bad arguments, or unreadable database.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
saphira-repo-state summary
.br
saphira-repo-state owner usr/bin/ssh
.br
saphira-repo-state user sshd
.br
saphira-repo-state audit
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-repo-migrate (8),
.BR saphira-accounts-bootstrap (8),
.BR ensure-identity (8),
.BR saphira-build (8)
